---
description: Apply the SecureFlow security workflow when changing input handling, identity, permissions, secrets, database queries, or OS commands.
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: false
---

For security-relevant work, load the installed `secureflow` skill and follow its six phases:
scope, risk identification, requirements and threat model, secure implementation, security
review, and evidence-based verification.

Do not report a control as passing without code or configuration evidence. Run the gate from
the installed skill when the project uses the supported C#/ASP.NET Core profile:

```bash
python .cursor/skills/secureflow/scripts/secureflow-gate.py scan --root . --report secureflow-report.json
```

Treat `UNVERIFIED` as unresolved work, not as success.
